{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/691059-trains-following-the-herds-bison-and-the-apis","id":691059,"title":"Trains following the Herds: Bison and the Apis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-06T05:43:53-07:00","id":691059,"title":"Trains following the Herds: Bison and the Apis","content":"&quot;Kinda sucks the Apis ended up being one of the few breeds who's Kinfolk where delicious.&quot; -Rolls in Muck, Bone Gnawer Galliard<br /> <br /> &quot;Ugh, that was a heartbreaker, they came so close to pulling it off too. I think the last of them was at the binding of the Storm Eater Bane, yknow? Old Man Manyskins told me about it, she was so old, blind from cataracts, stuck in whatever the cow version of Harano is...One day she just didn't get up from her chair, heart gave out...And frankly, I don't blame her one damn bit, even Coyote would be hard pressed to find some humor in this. But yknow, every so often we find weird hoofprints out in the Umbra, its possible a few still are our there, but boy is it unlikely.&quot; Runs in Cool Shadows, Nuswisha Umbral Danser <br /> <br /> Any Theurge and most Galliards would tell you that the Changing Breeds cannot endure without Beast Kinfolk. Fewer will tell you that a few of the Garou tribes have successfully bred with unusual canine liniages, the Red Talons have bred with Singing Dogs and African Wild Dogs, and of course the Bunyip bred with Tasmanian Tigers. What follows is a legend passed around certain Midwestern septs of Garou, a story about bitter loss and the crushing of one final hope.<br /> <br /> Until around 1500, a small amount of Apis existed in the Umbra. Watching their kin closely in hopes that the situation would change enough that they could repopulate their breed without aggravating the Garou. However, when the Aurochs started to die out around fifteen hundred, they began looking for other methods to preserve their species. The Midwives of Gaia would not accept extinction so easily, and refused to give up without a fight.<br /> <br /> It was then that the Apis drew the attention of one of the Corax, who informed them of 'great plains full of cattle' in the Pure Lands. What followed was an epic journey across the Umbral Oceans, the calling in of every favor the Apis breed had been owed by the spirit world, and the use of powerful rites to cross into the Pure Lands. Once they arrived, the handful of Wereaurochs made bargains with the Three Brothers, which where readily accepted as they where one of the first travelers to EVER come across the Atlantic (With the exception of a few Norsemen in the time of Lief Erickson, which...did not exactly end well for the Vikings.) <br /> <br /> The deal was simple, the Brothers would protect the secret of the Apis, they wouldn't tell the European Garou about the Apis's plans, and when the Apis recovered, they'd pick up their old duties of finding ideal mates for the Pure Ones. It seemed like a grand idea, and to be honest it probably was one of the few examples of a real give-and-take deal between the Changing Breeds in history. <br /> <br /> Using powerful rites earned from Incarnae Spirits during their umbral exile (Similar to the methods used by the Bunyip), the Apis managed to begin breeding with the American Bison, producing Buffalo kinfolk. Its said that the Apis wept for joy when they first determined a calf was indeed Kin to the Apis. Using their matchmaking skills, before long they had an entire herd of Kinfolk, and a small amount of Apis began to be born. By then, they'd heard whispering of 'Wyrmcomers', but the few Apis where too involved in their project to give it much thought, even when the <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Croatan </span></span>fell sealing away the Storm Eater Bane.<br /> <br /> Had they, however, they might of averted what was to come. <br /> <br /> One day, an Apis came across a carcass of a Buffalo, one of their Kinfolk. The native tribes had long been guided to avoid certain herds, and that aside, the killing didn't look like something the Natives would of done. Investigating, the Apis came across a strange sight, a ring of wagons on the Prairie with white men eating the meat of the Buffalo. He then returned to the other Apis, who spoke to the Garou Tribes<br /> <br /> &quot;Brothers, our Kin have been devoured by these Wyrmcomers, what do you make of this?&quot; they asked<br /> <br /> &quot;The white men want food, and know not the ways of the Prairie. We wish to help you, but the Middle Brother is gone now, and our own people are in danger. If we cannot help ourselves, then how can we help you? We are sorry, but we must preserve out own kin.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Apis nodded, and returned to the Prairie, in disappointment, but knowing that the Wendigo and the Uktena spoke true. If they did not preserve their own kin, then they would suffer the same fate the Apis did. And so, the Apis struggled to stem the flow of Settlers, but they where so few, and in a scarce few decades, 90 percent of the new Kinfolk had been eaten, shot for sport or hides, or simply killed to send their skulls back east as trophies. No new Apis where born, and the narrow hope that they might recover their species died out. <br /> <br /> As the 1800s went on, the few Apis who had lasted that long died of old age, or where picked off by spiritual threats, Black Spirals, and other enemies who exploited their weakness. The last of the Apis, the Lakota woman known as Lost Hope, was nearly a century old when the Storm Eater Bane was sealed. She gave the last of her strength to assist the Garou ritualists in binding it, then died of a broken heart, her only solace being that she would join her lost breed in death.<br /> <br /> However, perhaps all was not lost. The Humans, perhaps for the first time, noticed that they may of taken things a little too far. A few men, some of which where Kinfolk of the Pure Ones, gathered what few Buffalo remained, and began to breed them. It was slow going, for they lacked the skills of the Apis, but in time, the herds returned. And every so often, a White Buffalo is born to these herds, with some Uktena seers believing them to be a sign from Gaia that perhaps the Apis are not as dead has everybody believes them to be....Perhaps, in these last times before the Apocalypse, an Cow will give birth to another Apis in the depths of Yellowstone Park, and one of the greatest tragedies of the Changing Breeds might be reversed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:15:33-07:00","id":691386,"title":"","content":"Neat story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T14:51:42-07:00","id":691733,"title":"","content":"Very cool. This idea is both a nice way of incorporating a long dead changing breed in a western game while simultaneously hearkening back to the old 'Buffalo Woman' myths. I might have to include some of these 'last hold-out' bison shifters in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T20:29:45-07:00","id":693402,"title":"","content":"The opening quote alone makes this great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}